# Narrow edits

Match the request to one row. Read those paths only. Do not list the repo, open other tasks, or read `README.md` unless the user asked about docs.

| Request | Read |
| --- | --- |
| GlazeWM, tiling, workspaces, keybinds | `config/glazewm.yaml`, matching function in `tasks/GlazeWm.ps1` |
| Zebar bar | `config/zebar/index.html`, `config/zebar/zpack.json`, `config/zebar/volume.ps1` |
| Terminal | `config/terminal-settings.json`, `tasks/Terminal.ps1` |
| Packages | `config/packages.psd1`, `tasks/Packages.ps1` |
| Git, WSL, Node, Flow Launcher, Input Leap, appearance | that one file under `tasks/`, plus its `config/` file if the task copies one |
| Installer selection or elevation | `install.ps1` and the single task it calls |
| CI failure | the failing step in `.github/workflows/validate.yml` only |

- `git status --short` once. Keep unrelated user changes.
- After editing, grep the changed name in `tests/install.Tests.ps1`. Open a workflow file only when that grep hits it.
- Check syntax with the PowerShell parser on the edited script, or Prettier on the edited HTML file if `node_modules` already exists. Do not install Pester, PSScriptAnalyzer, or npm packages. Do not run the full test file.
- Edit `config/` in the repo. Do not touch `%USERPROFILE%\.glzr`, the registry, or running apps unless the user asked for a live change.
